      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to use the formula for projecting a vector \\(\\mathbf{v}\\) onto a vector \\(\\mathbf{u}\\):\n\\[\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{u}} \\mathbf{v} = \\frac{\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{u}}{\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{u}} \\mathbf{u}\n\\]\n\nGiven:\n\\[\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{u}} \\mathbf{v} = \\frac{12}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nWe need to find the unknown vector \\(\\mathbf{v}\\). The vector \\(\\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ z \\end{pmatrix}\\) is \\(\\mathbf{v}\\) and \\(\\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\\) is \\(\\mathbf{u}\\). \n\nFirst, let's denote:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ z \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\mathbf{u} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThe projection formula becomes:\n\\[\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{u}} \\mathbf{v} = \\frac{\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{u}}{\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{u}} \\mathbf{u}\n\\]\n\nNext, let's calculate the dot products:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{u} = (0 \\cdot -3) + (3 \\cdot 5) + (z \\cdot -1) = 0 + 15 - z = 15 - z\n\\]\n\\[\n\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{u} = (-3 \\cdot -3) + (5 \\cdot 5) + (-1 \\cdot -1) = 9 + 25 + 1 = 35\n\\]\n\nNow, substitute back into the projection formula:\n\\[\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{u}} \\mathbf{v} = \\frac{15 - z}{35} \\mathbf{u} = \\frac{12}{35} \\mathbf{u}\n\\]\n\nTo verify, compare:\n\\[\n\\frac{15 - z}{35} \\mathbf{u} = \\frac{12}{35} \\mathbf{u}\n\\]\n\nBy them, we get:\n\\[\n\\frac{15 - z}{35} = \\frac{12}{35}\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\(z\\):\n\\[\n15 - z = 12\n\\]\n\\[\nz = 3\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(z\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{3}\n\\]",
