      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine the value of \\( z \\), we need to use the formula for the projection of a vector \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) onto a vector \\(\\mathbf{b}\\), which is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{a} = \\frac{\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}}{\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{b}\n\\]\n\nwhere:\n- \\(\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}\\) is the dot product of \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{b}\\),\n- \\(\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}\\) is the dot product of \\(\\mathbf{b}\\) with itself.\n\nGiven:\n- The vector \\(\\mathbf{a} = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ z \\end{pmatrix}\\),\n- The vector \\(\\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\\),\n- The projection of \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) onto \\(\\mathbf{b}\\) is \\(\\frac{12}{35} \\mathbf{b}\\).\n\nFirst, we compute the dot product \\(\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = 0 \\cdot (-3) + 3 \\cdot 5 + z \\cdot (-1) = 0 + 15 - z = 15 - z\n\\]\n\nNext, we compute the dot product \\(\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = (-3) \\cdot (-3) + 5 \\cdot 5 + (-1) \\cdot (-1) = 9 + 25 + 1 = 35\n\\]\n\nNow, we can find the scalar component of the projection:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Scalar Component} = \\frac{15 - z}{35}\n\\]\n\nGiven that the projection is \\(\\frac{12}{35} \\mathbf{b}\\), we equate this to:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{15 - z}{35} \\mathbf{b} = \\frac{12}{35} \\mathbf{b}\n\\]\n\nSince \\(\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = 35\\), the scalar component must satisfy:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{15 - z}{35} = \\frac{12}{35}\n\\]\n\nSetting these equal, we solve for \\(z\\):\n\n\\[\n15 - z = 12\n\\]\n\n\\[\nz = 3\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( z \\) is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).",
